INTERNAL CHANGELOG. Never shown to a member. Play "What's new" stays
"Bug fixes and improvements." per the owner's standing instruction.

THE NOTIFICATION ICON — the only change since 1037

WHAT MEMBERS SAW
  Every push arrived with a blank white square in the status bar instead of
  any mark at all.

WHY
  Nothing was configured. There was no ic_notification drawable anywhere in
  the repository, and no default_notification_icon meta-data in the manifest.
  With no small icon declared, the messaging library falls back to the
  launcher icon - and since Android 5.0 the status bar flattens the small
  icon to its alpha mask, keeping only which pixels are opaque and discarding
  every colour. The launcher icon is fully opaque, so its mask is a solid
  rectangle. That is the white square. The image was never corrupt.

WHAT CHANGED
  - A monochrome mark - the camera aperture from the centre of the app logo,
    white on a fully transparent background - at all five densities
    (24dp: 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 px).
  - default_notification_icon and default_notification_color declared in the
    manifest, with the accent colour used to tint the icon in the shade.
  - Both are installed by the build itself, after the native project is
    generated, because that folder is not stored in the repository.

  1039 shipped an earlier glyph that read as a flower at real size. 1040
  replaces it with the classic iris, which is legible at 24dp.

HOW IT IS PROVEN, not assumed
  The build now opens the finished bundle and fails if the icon is not in it:
    - ic_notification present in the bundle resource table
    - default_notification_icon present in the bundled manifest
    - default_notification_color present in the bundled manifest
  This matters because the release build runs resource shrinking, which is
  free to drop a drawable that is only referenced from the manifest. Any
  future change that quietly strips the icon now stops at CI instead of
  reaching the store.

REGISTRATION
  Untouched. No app code, no web code and no database changed in this build.

